Locale data for NetSurf's Intl (Onyx), derived from the Unicode CLDR 48 as shipped in ICU 78 (the
IANA time zone rules: tz 2025c). Unicode License v3: LICENSE.

intl-data.txt is generated, not edited: tools/tests/netsurf/intl/gendata.js reads every string and
pattern back from the Intl of Node.js (full ICU: Chrome's data) by formatting probe values:

    node tools/tests/netsurf/intl/gendata.js > third_party/cldr-48/intl-data.txt

One record per line, "key<TAB>JSON" (lines starting with '#' are comments):
- meta: the locales, the currencies' digits, the units, the numbering systems, likely subtags...
- <locale>/<section>: n (numbers), d (dates), u (units), r (relative time), l (lists), dn
  (display names), z (time zone names). A regional locale (en-GB) keeps only the leaves that differ
  from its language's ("path": value).
- tz: every IANA zone's standard offset and current daylight-saving rule, the links.

The makefiles (user/netsurf/netsurf-app.mk, tools/tests/netsurf/host.mk) compile it into NetSurf
as a C string with intl.js (qjs_intl_js.h); intl.js parses a record at its first use. See
docs/06-NETSURF-CHANGES.md, "Intl".
